{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Proportional Editing in Blender Modeling.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Proportional Editing in Blender Modeling.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"proportional editing in blender modeling proportional editing in blender modeling","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Proportional Editing in Blender Modeling.md","fileName":"Proportional Editing in Blender Modeling.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Proportional Editing in Blender Modeling","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 01:18\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Mesh Shaping Tools]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Mesh Shaping Tools","creatinggameenvironmentsinblender3d.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Proportional Editing in Blender Modeling.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Proportional Editing in Blender Modeling.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"proportional editing in blender modeling proportional editing in blender modeling","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Proportional Editing in Blender Modeling.md","fileName":"Proportional Editing in Blender Modeling.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Proportional Editing in Blender Modeling","heading":"Proportional Editing in Blender Modeling","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Proportional editing extends a transform beyond the directly selected components through a distance-based falloff. Nearby vertices move strongly and distant vertices move less, creating a smooth regional deformation from a compact selection.\n\nFalloff shape and influence radius determine the character of the change, while connected-only behavior can prevent influence from crossing separate geometry. The technique supports terrain and organic shaping without manually selecting every affected vertex.","tags":["baby"],"links"